# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
good_will	one
pleasing_sight	one
worthy_of_happiness	one
# "Good will" means the same morally good disposition of the will in S2, S4, S5 and S6.
# "Happiness" in S6 is the same well-being and contentment S4 names, so "worthy of happiness" is used in one sense.
# A1 links two different claims (worthiness and the spectator's pleasure) and does not carry one word between two senses.
